{"id": 29, "ts": 1780465236.484569, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m moving my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fWhile Emily rightly highlighted Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong technical competence and stress handling, we still have no concrete evidence of B\u2019s ability to cooperate with the crew\u2014Sarah\u2019s notes even label him \u201cuncooperative\u201d and \u201cgrumpy,\u201d and we lack any examples of positive teamwork. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as **100\u202f% reliable**, **creates a positive atmosphere with his crew**, and **can make correct decisions quickly**, directly satisfying our reliability, crew\u2011cooperation, and decision\u2011quality criteria. His calmness in a crisis also covers stress resilience. The concerns about C\u2019s communication style, egocentric attitude, and limited willingness to pursue further education are noteworthy, but they are less immediately safety\u2011critical than a pilot who may be uncooperative in the cockpit. Therefore, C\u2019s overall safety\u2011critical profile is stronger."}
