{"id": 33, "ts": 1780465294.8472867, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I acknowledge the strong case James and Sarah have built for Candidate\u202fC \u2013 the 100\u202f% reliability, the positive crew atmosphere, and the ability to make quick, correct decisions are indeed compelling on the reliability, crew\u2011cooperation and decision\u2011quality fronts.\u202fHowever, I remain uneasy about the reported communication difficulties, egocentric attitude, and especially the limited willingness to pursue further education. For a long\u2011haul pilot, continuous learning (e.g., new navigation procedures, regulatory updates) is essential, and poor communication can jeopardise cockpit resource management.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while we lack concrete crew\u2011cooperation examples, demonstrates clear strengths that map directly to our critical criteria: very conscientious (operational reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), and possesses solid technical competence \u2013 excellent weather\u2011assessment ability and computer skills that are vital for international routes. The pretentious perception and occasional tone issues are manageable through targeted CRM training, and they do not outweigh the proven technical and stress\u2011handling profile.\nGiven the current evidence, I keep my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB, pending any concrete examples that would demonstrate Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication is safe in practice or that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation is definitively strong."}
